From e3d51ba3771cf7fd6feecfcf49701cfd55d66346 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bobsixsixsix-boop <304558835+bobsixsixsix-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:34:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] aw882xx: mute/unmute the amplifiers at trigger time (tb323fu)

ASoC calls mute_stream(0) at the end of prepare and mute_stream(1) in
hw_free (soc-pcm.c __soc_pcm_prepare / soc_pcm_hw_clean, v7.3-rc4).
On kaanapali's q6apm MI2S back end the bit clock is started by the back
end's TRIGGER_START (q6apm-lpass-dais.c q6apm_lpass_dai_trigger ->
q6apm_graph_start) and stopped by its next prepare
(q6apm_lpass_dai_prepare stops a started graph) or shutdown. So today:

- the start work (pwd off, PLL poll every 2 ms) runs before the clock
  exists; it only succeeds when TRIGGER_START follows within the 20 ms
  poll window, and the ACP profile probe (prepare, never started)
  produces the five 'pll&clk check fail / start failed' rounds at boot;
- an xrun recovery in PipeWire (snd_pcm_drop + snd_pcm_prepare +
  start, alsa-pcm.c alsa_recover) stops and restarts the back-end graph
  while the amplifiers stay powered and unmuted at full gain
  (aw882xx_start_pa returns 'already start').

With .mute_unmute_on_trigger the core unmutes each codec DAI right after
the CPU DAI's TRIGGER_START and mutes it before TRIGGER_STOP
(soc-dai.c snd_soc_pcm_dai_trigger), i.e. always with the clock running,
and an xrun recovery becomes a clean stop/start of the amplifiers.
The DPCM links are nonatomic (sound/soc/qcom/common.c), so the sleeping
aw882xx_mute() is allowed there.

Costs: aw882xx_mute(1) (device_stop, ~19 ms per amplifier, ~33 ms with
fade-flag) now runs inside snd_pcm_drop instead of snd_pcm_close; an
xrun now costs ~20-30 ms of amplifier restart. Not built, not run.
---
 kernel/out-of-tree/aw882xx/aw882xx.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/out-of-tree/aw882xx/aw882xx.c b/kernel/out-of-tree/aw882xx/aw882xx.c
index c69d968..3b473ca 100644
--- a/kernel/out-of-tree/aw882xx/aw882xx.c
+++ b/kernel/out-of-tree/aw882xx/aw882xx.c
@@ -440,6 +440,18 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dai_ops aw882xx_dai_ops = {
 	.set_sysclk = aw882xx_set_dai_sysclk,
 	.hw_params = aw882xx_hw_params,
 	.mute_stream = aw882xx_mute,
+	/*
+	 * tb323fu: unmute on TRIGGER_START / mute on TRIGGER_STOP instead of
+	 * prepare / hw_free. On the q6apm MI2S back end the bit clock only
+	 * runs between the back end's TRIGGER_START (graph start) and its next
+	 * prepare or shutdown (graph stop): with prepare-time unmuting the
+	 * start work polled the PLL before any clock existed (every
+	 * profile-probe open failed five times), and on an xrun recovery
+	 * (drop, prepare, start) the back end stopped the clock under a
+	 * powered, unmuted amplifier. The DPCM links are nonatomic
+	 * (qcom common.c), so aw882xx_mute() may sleep here.
+	 */
+	.mute_unmute_on_trigger = 1,
 	.shutdown = aw882xx_shutdown,
 };
 
